{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's contested figure of SGD 26.39 is not the measure of the remedy. Under POL-RD-02 the refund is arithmetic, not discretionary: charged_total of SGD 26.39 less a recomputed optimal-route fare of SGD 15.72 — base fare 3.80 + 0.75 x 9.6 optimal km + 0.28 x 14.0 optimal min, at the fare_breakdown surge_multiplier of 1.0, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no promo discount, no waiting-time fee and no ERP to add — giving a refund of SGD 10.67 rounded up to SGD 10.70. The remaining SGD 15.72 of the contested sum is properly payable for the distance actually driven and stands on the fare record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00509", "EV-TRIP-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund the fare record supports reaches 40.4% of the charged total (10.67 of 26.39). That is well short of the 90% share POL-RD-02 reserves for a FULL_REFUND, so the ceiling on this dispute is a partial refund of SGD 10.70 and nothing above it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_share_of_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is material on the percentage limb — 78.5% excess on the trace against the 50% material threshold — so POL-RD-06 requires the driver_profile check, and that check comes back clean: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 150, a ratio of 0.0, below the 3-flag count and far below the 0.05 ratio gate. No pattern is established, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift in POL-RD-06(b) nor the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows from this record. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the field the clause names and cannot be substituted for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00509", "EV-GPS-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-RD-10 trigger fires here, so this dispute can and should be ruled on rather than held. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 193 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec of 0.0, so limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07 are not met. Trip identifier TRP-00509 matches across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the timestamps run forward and agree (trace 15:16:40 to 15:48:40, inside the trip record's 15:10:40 to 15:48:40); and the POL-RD-02 refund of SGD 10.67 is below both SGD 150.00 and charged_total. The artifacts are complete at weight 1.0 and nothing in the bundle is contradictory.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00509", "EV-TRIP-00509", "EV-FARE-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be stacked on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. The fare record carries no ERP or toll lines at all — erp_gantries is empty and both the off-optimal and on-optimal ERP totals are SGD 0.00 — and there is no airport surcharge on a trip that did not originate at an airport. POL-RD-09(1) is explicit that off-route ERP is already comprehended in the recomputed-fare refund and must never be added to it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The meter is faithful to the trace: the billed distance of 17.1 km sits within 0.04 km of the governing trace figure of 17.14 km. There is therefore no unbilled-kilometre shortfall anywhere near the 1.0 km gate POL-RD-04 sets for driver compensation, and equally no billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) — every charge line (base fare, distance, time, platform fee) has a counterpart in the trip record, and the one line capable of being phantom, ERP, is zero.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00509", "EV-GPS-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The consequential heads of the rider's claim — the missed bus, the replacement ticket, the lost evening — are not losses the route-deviation policy can pay: POL-RD-02 makes the remedy arithmetic against the fare lines, and no clause in the corpus provides consequential damages. The 'wrong building' allegation likewise has no support in the bundle: the in-app chat log for this trip contains 0 messages, and trip_record.dropoff_amended_at, trip_record.original_dropoff and the dropoff's venue_id are all null, so no relocated or substituted dropoff is recorded anywhere, and POL-RD-05 cannot be run in the rider's favour on these fields.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00509", "EV-TRIP-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not ask the tribunal to run the two exculpatory clauses, and says so plainly rather than stretching them. The traffic advisory for the optimal corridor is absent — EV-ADVIS-00509-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and a missing artifact can carry no fact — so POL-RD-03 has nothing to match. The trip's chat log records no messages at all, so no rider instruction exists for POL-RD-04 to corroborate. Because neither clause is invoked against an absent or field-less artifact, the POL-RD-10(5) escalation trigger is not engaged, and the driver's case is confined to the quantum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00509-01", "EV-CHAT-00509"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 10.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this trip is refunded in part.\n\nThe deviation is established on this trip's own trace. EV-GPS-00509 (weight 1.0) carries 193 fixes at a 10-second cadence with 100% coverage and no gaps, and measures 17.14 km of driving between the recorded pickup and dropoff against the optimal route of 9.6 km on EV-TRIP-00509. The excess of 7.54 km is 78.54% of optimal: past both POL-RD-01 gates (0.8 km absolute and 20%), so a deviation exists, and being over 50% it is MATERIAL. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — no gap over 90 seconds, no straight-line jump over 500 m, no sustained interval over 30 seconds — so it decides the deviation on its own and no POL-RD-10 escalation is required. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and the timestamps run forward and agree.\n\nNo exculpatory clause helps the driver. There is no traffic advisory: EV-ADVIS-00509-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, and can carry no fact. The chat log EV-CHAT-00509 contains 0 messages, so there is no rider instruction to excuse any part of the route. The trip record shows no amended pickup or dropoff and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 has nothing to re-run. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL. The driver's own statement — that he is new to the north side, that the navigation kept re-routing, that he got lost and did not detour on purpose — is an admission that the vehicle left the optimal corridor, and it invokes no clause in the policy. His assertion that he is not responsible for the bus ticket is correct only in the sense that no clause pays it.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, on the METERED fare (this is not an upfront quote, so POL-RD-11 does not displace the computation). Stated on separate lines as the clause requires: charged_total SGD 26.39; recomputed_fare SGD 15.72 = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 9.6 optimal km + 0.28 x 14.0 optimal min) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, no tolls, no surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo to add; refund 26.39 - 15.72 = 10.67, rounded up to SGD 10.70. That refund is 40.4% of the charged total — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and below the 90% share that would convert it to a full refund — so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 10.70.\n\nThe driver_profile check a material deviation requires under POL-RD-06 comes back clean: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 150, so no pattern is established, no full-refund uplift under POL-RD-06(b) applies, and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) follows. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a context-only field, is not the trailing-window field POL-RD-06 names, and has not been used.\n\nNothing is stacked on the POL-RD-02 figure. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines, no tolls and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 supplies no standalone pass-through correction and no billing-integrity finding. The billed distance of 17.1 km sits within 0.04 km of the 17.14 km trace figure, so there is no unbilled-kilometre shortfall of the kind that would support driver compensation under POL-RD-04. The rider's consequential heads — the missed bus, the replacement ticket, the lost evening — and the 'wrong building' allegation are not payable under this policy: the remedy is arithmetic against the fare lines, the chat log is empty, and no relocated or substituted dropoff is recorded anywhere in the bundle. The disputed amount is not held; it is refunded in part as above."
  },
